    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Confidence of the Foolish"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "To the Chief Musician. A Psalm of the sons of Korah."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Hear this, all peoples;",
          "Give ear, all inhabitants of the world,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Both low and high,",
          "Rich and poor together."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My mouth shall speak wisdom,",
          "And the meditation of my heart shall give understanding."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will incline my ear to a proverb;",
          "I will disclose my dark saying on the harp."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why should I fear in the days of evil,",
          "When the iniquity at my heels surrounds me?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Those who trust in their wealth",
          "And boast in the multitude of their riches,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "None of them can by any means redeem his brother,",
          "Nor give to God a ransom for him—"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the redemption of their souls is costly,",
          "And it shall cease forever—"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "That he should continue to live eternally,",
          "And not see the Pit."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For he sees wise men die;",
          "Likewise the fool and the senseless person perish,",
          "And leave their wealth to others."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Their inner thought is that their houses will last forever,",
          "Their dwelling places to all generations;",
          "They call their lands after their own names."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Nevertheless man, though in honor, does not remain;",
          "He is like the beasts that perish."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "This is the way of those who are foolish,",
          "And of their posterity who approve their sayings."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Like sheep they are laid in the grave;",
          "Death shall feed on them;",
          "The upright shall have dominion over them in the morning;",
          "And their beauty shall be consumed in the grave, far from their dwelling."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But God will redeem my soul from the power of the grave,",
          "For He shall receive me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Do not be afraid when one becomes rich,",
          "When the glory of his house is increased;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For when he dies he shall carry nothing away;",
          "His glory shall not descend after him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though while he lives he blesses himself",
          "(For men will praise you when you do well for yourself),"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He shall go to the generation of his fathers;",
          "They shall never see light."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A man who is in honor, yet does not understand,",
          "Is like the beasts that perish."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
